TITLE:: MaplinSM333
summary:: B-Format Ambisonic Spatial Enhancement Processor
categories:: UGens>Ambisonic
related:: Classes/FoaEncode, Classes/FoaDecode, Classes/AmbiVerbSC

DESCRIPTION::
MaplinSM333 is a B-format ambisonic spatial enhancement processor that simulates the Maplin SM-333 Surround Sound Matrix in the ambisonic domain. It works directly with B-format signals (WXYZ) and is compatible with any ambisonic encoder input, making it suitable for use with UHJ, Superstereo, or other ambisonic encoders.

The processor enhances spatial difference signals by applying multi-stage all-pass filtering, frequency-dependent delays, and subtle saturation to create a vintage surround sound effect. It primarily works on the directional components (X, Y) while preserving the omnidirectional character of the W component.

The effect can be used as an optional spatial enhancement stage in any ambisonic processing chain, providing vintage-style surround sound enhancement without the channel mismatch issues of traditional stereo-to-quad conversion.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Main audio rate processing method.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

ARGUMENT:: surround
Surround enhancement level (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.8).

ARGUMENT:: effect
Effect intensity level (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.8).

ARGUMENT:: delay
Delay time control (0.0 to 1.0, maps to 5-50ms, default 0.4).

ARGUMENT:: active
Bypass/Active control (0.0 = bypass, 1.0 = active, default 1).

ARGUMENT:: saturation
Op-amp saturation amount (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.15).

ARGUMENT:: noise
Thermal noise level (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.1).

ARGUMENT:: bandwidth
Bandwidth limiting control (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.5).

ARGUMENT:: bbdNoise
BBD (Bucket Brigade Device) noise level (0.0 to 1.0, default 0.1).

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals [W, X, Y, Z].

METHOD:: balanced
Convenience method with balanced preset configuration.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals with balanced settings.

METHOD:: maximum
Convenience method with maximum effect preset configuration.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals with maximum effect settings.

METHOD:: subtle
Convenience method with subtle effect preset configuration.

ARGUMENT:: input
A 4-element array containing B-format components [W, X, Y, Z].

returns:: A 4-element array of processed B-format signals with subtle effect settings.


EXAMPLES::

code::
// Basic usage in a SynthDef
(
SynthDef(\maplinExample, { |in, out|
    var bformat, processed;
    
    // Create B-format from stereo input
    bformat = FoaEncode.ar(SoundIn.ar([0, 1]), FoaEncoderKernel.newUHJ);
    
    // Apply Maplin processing
    processed = MaplinSM333.ar(bformat, 
        surround: 0.8, 
        effect: 0.8, 
        delay: 0.4, 
        active: 1
    );
    
    // Decode to stereo
    Out.ar(out, FoaDecode.ar(processed, FoaDecoderKernel.newListen));
}).add;
)

// Start the synth
Synth(\maplinExample);
::

code::
// Using preset configurations
(
SynthDef(\maplinPresets, { |in, out, preset = 0|
    var bformat, processed;
    
    bformat = FoaEncode.ar(SoundIn.ar([0, 1]), FoaEncoderKernel.newUHJ);
    
    // Select preset based on control
    processed = Select.kr(preset, [
        MaplinSM333.balanced(bformat),
        MaplinSM333.maximum(bformat),
        MaplinSM333.subtle(bformat)
    ]);
    
    Out.ar(out, FoaDecode.ar(processed, FoaDecoderKernel.newListen));
}).add;
)

// Start with different presets
Synth(\maplinPresets, [\preset, 0]); // Balanced
Synth(\maplinPresets, [\preset, 1]); // Maximum
Synth(\maplinPresets, [\preset, 2]); // Subtle
::

code::
// Integration with existing ambisonic chain
(
SynthDef(\fullAmbisonicChain, { |in, out, maplinActive = 1, maplinSurround = 0.8|
    var bformat, eqed, maplinProcessed, ambient, decoded;
    
    // Encode to B-format
    bformat = FoaEncode.ar(SoundIn.ar([0, 1]), FoaEncoderKernel.newUHJ);
    
    // Apply EQ (example)
    eqed = bformat.collect({ |channel, i|
        BPeakEQ.ar(channel, 1000, 1, 3.dbamp);
    });
    
    // Apply Maplin processing (can be bypassed)
    maplinProcessed = MaplinSM333.ar(eqed, 
        surround: maplinSurround,
        active: maplinActive
    );
    
    // Add ambience
    ambient = AmbiVerbSC.ar(maplinProcessed, mix: 0.3);
    
    // Decode to stereo
    decoded = FoaDecode.ar(ambient, FoaDecoderKernel.newListen);
    
    Out.ar(out, decoded);
}).add;
)

// Start with Maplin active
Synth(\fullAmbisonicChain, [\maplinActive, 1, \maplinSurround, 0.8]);
::

code::
// Real-time parameter control
(
var synth, window, controls;
synth = Synth(\maplinExample);

window = Window("MaplinSM333 Controls", Rect(100, 100, 300, 200)).front;
controls = CompositeView(window, Rect(10, 10, 280, 180));

// Surround control
EZSlider(controls, Rect(10, 10, 260, 20), "Surround", \amp.asSpec, 
    { |slider| synth.set(\surround, slider.value) }, 0.8);

// Effect control  
EZSlider(controls, Rect(10, 40, 260, 20), "Effect", \amp.asSpec,
    { |slider| synth.set(\effect, slider.value) }, 0.8);

// Delay control
EZSlider(controls, Rect(10, 70, 260, 20), "Delay", \amp.asSpec,
    { |slider| synth.set(\delay, slider.value) }, 0.4);

// Active/Bypass toggle
Button(controls, Rect(10, 100, 80, 30))
    .states_([["BYPASS", Color.red, Color.black], ["ACTIVE", Color.green, Color.black]])
    .action_({ |btn| synth.set(\active, btn.value) })
    .value_(1);
)
:: 